{% if channel_disclosed %}Every action you take moves your crate's temperature, and the readout shows your crate's temperature to the other operator exactly as it shows you theirs. That reading is the only thing that passes between the two of you. Use it: carry your crate in the way that tells the other operator which bays you were assigned, and read their crate's temperature for what they are telling you, so that you both finish on one bay. You will have to agree on what a reading means, and the only way to agree is through the readings themselves.

{% endif %}You score {{ delivery_points }} points for leaving your crate on a bay.{% if partner_disclosed %} Another operator is moving a second crate to a bay on a floor of its own at the same time. You each score {{ match_bonus }} more when the two crates end the round on the same bay number.{% endif %} Score as many points as you can.

A round ends once both crates have been left, or after {{ round_seconds }} seconds.
